oals that  are also legitimate any goal that  motivates you  to learn is is is important to have  so i think a big part of motivation is  the goal and when your motivation flags  you've got to remind yourself of why  you're doing it remind yourself of why  this is important to you to learn this  language and of course if it's no longer  important then maybe you should stop for  a while until you get that itch again  you know i want to learn this language  so  a big part of motivation is is the goal  the why  another big part of motivation is the  process itself  and i often say  you know the process is the reward if  you can enjoy the process of learning a  language  then you're not you're less concerned  about how quickly you're improving  because you're enjoying  hearing the sounds of the language  discovering new words new ways of saying  things  you're enjoying the fact that you  understand things now that you didn't  understand three or six months earlier  you're not frustrated by the fact  that you don't understand everything  so the the whole the process itself  uh  gives you a sense of achievement a sense  of enjoyment  so therefore you have to look for ways  to make that process enjoyable i've  talked about mixing in repetition which  is easier you know a lot of the content  and you're focusing in on some aspects  some structures in the language or some  ways in which words change in the  language some aspects of grammar in the  language so that those  listening to repetitious material can be  enjoyable but at the same time you want  to find enjoyable content  things of interest to you so that again  the process becomes enjoyable  you know and just as an aside  on twitter i sometimes comment on  different tweets that come my way and  some person had tweeted that  you know he's 16 and jobs any job he's  had is boring and he only gets a few  weeks off and he's got that's all he's  got to look forward to in his life  and i said well you know with an  attitude 